{"name":"Guava Juice","hex":"#f4b694","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"guava","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tropical tree or shrub of the myrtle family, Psidium guajava.","Its yellowish tropical fruit, globular or pear-shaped with thin, yellow, green or brown skin, is often made into jams and jellies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guava"},{"term":"juice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A liquid made from plant, especially fruit.","A beverage made of juice."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To extract the juice from something.","To energize or stimulate something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/juice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Guava Juice","blocks":[{"text":"Roi Allan Gille Fabito, better known as Guava Juice, is a Filipino-American YouTuber, actor and internet personality. He is known for his kid-friendly challenge videos, and formerly as half of the sketch-comedy duo Wassabi Productions with Alex Wassabi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Guava_Juice_2025_01.png/330px-Guava_Juice_2025_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guava_Juice","wikidata":"Q123567510"},{"title":"Guava","blocks":[{"text":"Guava, also known as the 'guava-pear' in various regions, is a common tropical fruit cultivated in many tropical and subtropical regions. The common guava Psidium guajava is a small tree in the myrtle family (Myrtaceae), native to Mexico, Central America, the Caribbean and northern South America. Botanically, guavas are berries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Guava_pink_fruit.jpg/330px-Guava_pink_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guava","wikidata":"Q3181909"},{"title":"Juice","blocks":[{"text":"Juice is a drink made from the extraction or pressing of the natural liquid contained in fruit and vegetables. It can also refer to liquids that are flavored with concentrate or other biological food sources like meat or seafood, such as clam juice. Juice is commonly consumed as a beverage or used as an ingredient or flavoring in foods or other beverages, such as smoothies. Juice emerged as a popular beverage choice after the development of pasteurization methods enabled its preservation without using fermentation. The largest fruit juice consumers are New Zealand and Colombia. Fruit juice consumption on average increases with a country's income level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Orange_juice_1.jpg/330px-Orange_juice_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juice","wikidata":"Q8492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Guava_Juice_2018.png/500px-Guava_Juice_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Guava_Juice_2018.png/500px-Guava_Juice_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fabito in 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuava_Juice_2018.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Guava_fruit_tree.jpg/500px-Guava_fruit_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Guava_fruit_tree.jpg/500px-Guava_fruit_tree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Guava fruit tree","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuava_fruit_tree.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Guava_flowers_%286700015761%29.jpg/250px-Guava_flowers_%286700015761%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1